{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787076420216141514,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cranial-goodly-seahog","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e022911cd6b1bc77b8ce481216dbdaed46f7b71333c2d528c0ce906ec8f40e94","event_uuid":"3d8e12f1-37fc-4adf-a25a-b88b25161c8c","position":{"commit_sha":"c9aa556f00baeb0cfc8b44a13496014a5adef188","position":"1787069744012918001-3d8e12f1-37fc-4adf-a25a-b88b25161c8c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6cba2767976cb2b83f1713eee14bc2e73efde17d837e5d7e4807d12a97d32375","event_uuid":"67c98a73-ff42-4f45-be59-6f3fad14003e","position":{"commit_sha":"46211f79d68bce62e9515b3350dd6bb949572a22","position":"1787069778612846001-67c98a73-ff42-4f45-be59-6f3fad14003e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0994b853408c2839fafa331dc9f6abda14c0452514fe92c9406a23eb14c50987","event_uuid":"a26337f7-ffda-49e6-a489-ca626552e5ed","position":{"commit_sha":"d1886e86a68f9570a0cbb6e57d3342032a85a305","position":"1787069999849017001-a26337f7-ffda-49e6-a489-ca626552e5ed"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6719a7ddf67c529e1377b9c4cc09aa98e32e2edc06d80a29d03a131aecc8d732","event_uuid":"183cf59d-d0dc-4bd0-a167-a049129c92a2","position":{"commit_sha":"cdd9cb7ec603a870283a4ec0b7ce1d14e63fb578","position":"1787070627531119001-183cf59d-d0dc-4bd0-a167-a049129c92a2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0dbaa7ed92ec092043fe7f3ff25a714c864aa59f56548d1b6ec87ff5eb423351","event_uuid":"f9ed11d5-4372-49b9-aeb2-51da4112de99","position":{"commit_sha":"ec12f70cf22ebdc2ffea46627608141e4991705f","position":"1787071932841869001-f9ed11d5-4372-49b9-aeb2-51da4112de99"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Analysis pass: building a code-v3 calibrator (segmented to impact_model_version=code-v3) in the session workspace to produce the per-criterion threshold report first. Corpus scoped: 1760 code_review_result_v2 sidecars / 1109 distinct change_ids (280 with >1 revision) / ~4284 findings. coverage.routing is empty for code-review so fire-rate uses a per-review fired/total proxy (noted as a caveat). Landing the harness under docs/experiments/ + any criteria_routing.json change will go through claim -> review-plan -> Gerrit once the recommendation is agreed.","timestamp":1787069778612846001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration complete (code-v3, 1760 sidecars / 1173 changes / 4359 findings). Recommendation (precision-first; EVERY would-block finding validity>=0.95, none <0.5):\n\nFLIP TO BLOCKING:\n- regression @ 0.54 (n=307, val 0.83, drop 0.17, rev_rr 0.68/93eps; blocks 2.81% of changes)\n- api-compat @ 0.51 (n=118, val 0.88, rev_rr 0.75/34eps; 0.77%)\n- deletion-impact @ 0.60 (n=73, val 0.88, rev_rr 0.66/21eps; 0.26%)\n- error-handling @ 0.50 (n=238, val 0.83, rev_rr 0.64/55eps; 0.26%, low-yield but precise)\n\nHOLD ADVISORY: performance (rev_rr 0.85 rests on only 12 episodes; would block 1 finding — insufficient evidence).\nKEEP: security @ 0.54 as-is (code-v3 confirms precise, 0.26% of changes). High-volume tests/maintainability/correctness/edge-cases stay advisory (rev_rr<0.6, blocking the ~0.30 priority mode = high friction).\nKEEP ADVISORY (FP-prone, high decider drop): docs 76%, supply-chain 64%, scope-intent 58%.\nNOT TUNABLE (DET/attestation): bugfix-size-attestation, secret-detection, sec.\n\nCaveat: a held-out (human/Sonnet) adjudication of the would-block sets should confirm before flipping in production, exactly as code-v2 deferred security to sibling b9c0. Full report + harness in session workspace. Landing (harness -> docs/experiments/, criteria_routing.json edits) pending operator go-ahead + the claim->review-plan->Gerrit workflow.","timestamp":1787069999849017001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Escaped-bug analysis (43 close_class=regression bugs, correlated to prior PASS reviews of the buggy file with defect-level identifier matching):\n\n(a) Would non-blocking findings have caught them? A finding existed for 8/43, but only 1/8 would flip to a BLOCK under the APPROVED thresholds:\n- autumnal-defectible-xeme ('rebar metrics' with no dates crashes): advisory regression prio 0.60 >= 0.54 -> WOULD BLOCK. Validates the regression flip.\n- The other 7 sat at prio 0.0-0.30 or were DROPPED by the Pass-3 decider (brattish-ladyish-jaguar: correct finding dropped at val 0.43). Threshold-tightening is NOT the lever for that tail.\nTwo non-threshold levers surfaced: (i) verifier RECALL (correct-but-dropped findings on regression/edge-cases); (ii) a targeted impact boost for deletion-impact/api-compat findings that cite a removed public symbol + a named broken caller (citric-preregal-ladybird sat at 0.30, below the 0.60/0.51 flips).\n\n(b) Criteria gaps (recurring escaped classes with NO relevant finding): import/packaging resolution integrity (~4), CI-gate rollout backward-compat (~4), CLI<->MCP<->import-format surface parity (~3; halfwhite-chordal-stonefly had 9 PASS reviews and zero findings), live/external-integration signatures (~4, out of scope for static review). Proposing new overlays: import-integrity (or expand deletion-impact to import-graph breakage), surface-parity, ci-gate-compat. Full report in session workspace.","timestamp":1787070627531119001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDING (local, validated — not yet pushed to Gerrit). Applied the four approved code-v3 threshold flips to src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json:\n- api-compat: advisory -> blocking@0.51 (overlay, already routed)\n- deletion-impact: advisory -> blocking@0.60 (content-triggered overlay)\n- regression: ADDED as blocking@0.54 (BASE reviewer dimension, exec:AGENT/applies_to:[] inert; only posture/threshold/blocking_enabled consulted by threshold_for)\n- error-handling: ADDED as blocking@0.50 (BASE dimension, same mechanism)\n\nMechanism verified: registry.threshold_for resolves (0.51/0.60/0.54/0.50, True) for each; base dims are picked up by threshold_for but ignored by det_criteria/glob_triggered_overlays/content_triggered_overlays (confirmed unchanged). Resolution is min-threshold/any-enabled, so a multi-tagged finding (e.g. [correctness, regression]) now blocks at 0.54; [correctness] alone stays advisory (0.95, False).\n\nUpdated 3 deliberate governance-pin tests to the newly-approved blocking set {secret-detection, high-critical-security, security, api-compat, deletion-impact, regression, error-handling}: test_impact_model_versioning.py, test_code_review_ws2.py, test_code_review_deletion_impact.py. Full targeted sweep: 713 passed (code_review/routing/criteria/decide/blocking/impact_model).\n\nDeliverables copied to docs/experiments/: calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py, code-review-threshold-calibration.md, escaped_bug_analysis.py, escaped-bug-review-gap-analysis.md.\n\nREMAINING: the Gerrit landing ceremony (set file_impact, review-plan attestation to claim, fresh worktree off origin/main, make lint, commit with rebar-ticket trailer + -s, push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main, LLM-Review+1 AND Verified+1, submit, then close). Pausing here for operator go-ahead on the external push.","timestamp":1787071932841869001}],"created_at":1787069744012918001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"Analyze the code-v3 code-review REVIEW_RESULT sidecar corpus (1760 sidecars / ~4284 findings, schema code_review_result_v2) to calibrate per-criterion block thresholds. Current criteria_routing.json blocks only on security (0.54, derived from the retired 114-sidecar code-v2 corpus by docs/experiments/derive_code_review_threshold.py) plus the two DET security detectors; every LLM criterion is advisory@0.95. \n\nBuild a code-v3 calibrator (analog of docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py, segmented by impact_model_version=code-v3) reporting per criterion: n, fire-rate, mean validity, P(dropped), P(indeterminate), revision-response (criterion-load-delta across Gerrit revisions of the same change_id), surviving-priority percentiles, and worst verifier sub-question. Emit a precision-first per-criterion threshold proposal + a written report. Recommendations only; flipping any criterion to blocking on production requires operator sign-off (as the code-v2 derivation deferred security to sibling b9c0).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0","ticket_type":"task","title":"Calibrate code-review criteria thresholds against the code-v3 sidecar corpus","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3d8e12f1-37fc-4adf-a25a-b88b25161c8c","67c98a73-ff42-4f45-be59-6f3fad14003e","a26337f7-ffda-49e6-a489-ca626552e5ed","183cf59d-d0dc-4bd0-a167-a049129c92a2","f9ed11d5-4372-49b9-aeb2-51da4112de99"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787076420216141514,"uuid":"11d5b6aa-ef40-4f36-8f40-3bb6d9fccaa1"}